From b140d34bcc08fb7d7bbfb2ef9969911510b6589d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Flack <flackr@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] [M156] Forbid CSSAnimations::Cancel during animated
 style and update passes

Original change's description:
> Forbid CSSAnimations::Cancel during animated style and update passes
>
> Flat-tree traversals while computing animated styles
> (StyleResolver::ApplyAnimatedStyle) or applying pending animation and
> timeline updates (PostStyleUpdateScope::ApplyAnimations) must operate on
> clean slot assignments and a stable flat tree. If a shadow root's slot
> assignment is unexpectedly left dirty entering those passes, lazy slot
> recalculation in Node::AssignedSlot() can detach unslotted subtrees and
> call CSSAnimations::Cancel() mid-iteration, clearing timeline and
> animation maps while they are being traversed.
>
> Track StyleEngine::InApplyAnimatedStyleScope alongside
> InApplyAnimationUpdateScope (including on child documents whose pending
> updates are drained by an outer PostStyleUpdateScope) and CHECK in
> CSSAnimations::Cancel() that neither pass is active.
>
> Bug: 584687200
> Change-Id: If5b4ea53471ba89aa016a72fa36ef8b4972cafe0
